 IFT, Ultrasound, Russian current and other therapeutic modalities explained.',\n      icon: 'flash',\n      iconBg: '#00ACC1',\n      level: 'Intermediate',\n      duration: '7 hours',\n      lessons: [{\n        id: 1,\n        title: 'Introduction to Electrotherapy',\n        duration: '25 min',\n        type: 'lesson',\n        image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1576091160550-2173dba999ef?w=600',\n        content: `Electrotherapy Basics\n\nUnderstanding the principles and applications of electrical modalities in physiotherapy.\n\nCommon Modalities:\n• TENS (Transcutaneous Electrical Nerve Stimulation)\n• IFT (Interferential Therapy)\n• Therapeutic Ultrasound\n• Russian Current\n• NMES (Neuromuscular Electrical Stimulation)\n\nSelection Criteria:\n• Treatment goals\n• Tissue type\n• Acuity of condition\n• Contraindications`\n      }]\n    },\n    'exercise-rx': {\n      title: 'Exercise Prescription',\n      description: 'Evidence-based exercise prescription for rehabilitation and performance enhancement.',\n      icon: 'dumbbell',\n      iconBg: '#5E35B1',\n      level: 'Advanced',\n      duration: '8 hours',\n      lessons: [{\n        id: 1,\n        title: 'Principles of Exercise Prescription',\n        duration: '30 min',\n        type: 'lesson',\n        image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517836357463-d25dfeac3438?w=600',\n        content: `Exercise Prescription\n\nLearn the FITT principle and how to design effective rehabilitation programs.\n\nFITT Principle:\n• Frequency - How often\n• Intensity - How hard\n• Time - How long\n• Type - What kind\n\nProgression Principles:\n• Gradual overload\n• Specificity\n• Individualization\n• Recovery periods`\n      }]\n    },\n    'sports-psych-course': {\n      title: 'Sports Psychology Basics',\n      description: 'Mental skills training, anxiety management, and performance optimization techniques.',\n      icon: 'head-heart',\n      iconBg: '#D81B60',\n      level: 'Beginner',\n      duration: '3 ho